# Shell scripts must be LF, always.
#
# .github/scripts/commit-and-push.sh runs on ubuntu-latest. Committed with CRLF
# it fails as `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` — which reads
# like a broken runner rather than a line-ending problem, on a job that only
# executes when data actually changed. This pins the ending at the repo level so
# it does not depend on each contributor's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated data is committed and diffed by the refresh workflows. Normalising
# it keeps a contributor's editor from rewriting whole files as CRLF and turning
# a one-line data change into a 40,000-line diff.
*.json text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
